@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: why proveo declines sbx's MCP gateway by default, and how a decline is expressed
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go (MCPGatewayVar, WithMCPGatewayPolicy,
'         DeclineMCPGateway, MCPGatewayAllowed)
' covers: internal/posture/posture.go (MCPGateway)
'   the Kit this rides in ......... _spec/internal/sbx/sbx-kit-contract.puml
'   the backend that writes it .... _spec/internal/sbx/sandbox-backend.puml
'   the home the entry would land in _spec/internal/proveohome/proveo-home-lifecycle.puml
'   one eliminated hypothesis ..... _spec/internal/sbx/seed-node-version-abort.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT THE GATEWAY IS, AND WHY IT IS NOT PROVEO'S ────────────────────────
' sbx's built-in agent kits register an MCP aggregator inside the sandbox:
'   claude mcp add mcp-gateway <url> --scope user
' Their setup step is gated on one variable — `[ -n "$MCP_GATEWAY_URL" ] || exit 0`
' — so declaring MCP_GATEWAY_URL EMPTY is the SUPPORTED way to decline. Nothing is
' patched, and there is no race with a step that runs inside the sandbox.
'
' ── USER SCOPE IS THE PROBLEM, NOT MCP ─────────────────────────────────────
' `--scope user` writes into the agent's home. proveo mounts the proveo home
' read-write, so an entry meant to live and die with a disposable sandbox lands in
' the operator's REAL home and outlives every run that wrote it.
'
' Worse than untidy: nothing in `proveo run --print` ever named it, which makes the
' gateway a THIRD source of agent capability beside the Kit's allowlist and the
' credential store — one the operator never saw and cannot audit from the plan.
'
' ── DECLINING COSTS NOTHING TODAY ──────────────────────────────────────────
' `sbx mcp ls` registers no servers, so the gateway currently aggregates an empty
' set: the decline removes an unaudited capability and no reach.
' PROVEO_SBX_MCP=on restores it, for an operator who has registered servers of
' their own and wants the agent to reach them.
'
' ── THE DECLINE IS DECLARED TWICE, ON PURPOSE ──────────────────────────────
' The Kit's environment block is the posture proveo PUBLISHES; the `-e` flag is
' what sandboxd applies when it CREATES the sandbox, which is the moment sbx's own
' injection happens. Either one alone may lose that race; neither is harmful when
' the other wins, so both are written.
'
' The Kit side is written EXPLICITLY rather than through KitEnvVars, because
' KitEnvVars drops empty values — and here the empty string IS the instruction.
' That same drop is what keeps the `-e` pair from duplicating the Kit's
' declaration: one mechanism, used in both directions.
'
' ── AND IT IS A POSTURE ROW ────────────────────────────────────────────────
' A posture that lists reachable hosts and credentials but NOT an MCP server the
' agent is told to call is not describing the run. posture.MCPGateway takes the
' backend and the decision as VALUES; it used to read PROVEO_SBX_MCP itself, which
' made the row a second place the decision was made rather than a rendering of the
' one the run already made.
title sbx MCP gateway — declined by default, and declared twice so it sticks

participant "operator" as OP <<app>>
participant "sandbox.Spec" as SPEC <<app>>
participant "Kit spec.yaml\nenvironment block" as KIT <<data>>
participant "sbx run -e\napplied at CREATE" as CLI <<host>>
participant "sbx built-in agent kit\nsetup step" as SETUP <<cloud>>
participant "the operator's proveo home\nmounted read-write" as HOME <<db>>

OP ARROW_MAIN SPEC : PROVEO_SBX_MCP unset (the default)
SPEC ARROW_MAIN KIT : MCP_GATEWAY_URL = "" (written explicitly)
SPEC ARROW_MAIN CLI : -e MCP_GATEWAY_URL=
KIT ARROW_QUEUE SETUP : the gate reads empty
CLI ARROW_QUEUE SETUP : the gate reads empty
SETUP ARROW_OPTIONAL SETUP : exit 0 — no registration
SETUP ARROW_ERROR HOME : what --scope user would have written

note over SETUP
  **The decline is the kit's own gate.**
  ""[ -n '$MCP_GATEWAY_URL' ] || exit 0"" is sbx's
  step, so an empty value is the supported way
  out — no patching, and no race with something
  running inside the sandbox.
end note

note over HOME
  **""--scope user"" outlives the sandbox.**
  proveo mounts the proveo home read-write, so an
  entry meant to die with a disposable VM lands in
  the operator's real home instead.
end note

note over HOME
  **Unaudited is the sharper half.** No
  ""proveo run --print"" ever named it, making the
  gateway a third source of agent capability
  beside the Kit allowlist and the credential
  store.
end note

note over KIT
  **The empty string IS the instruction.**
  ""KitEnvVars"" drops empty values, so this pair
  is written explicitly — and the same drop is
  what stops the ""-e"" copy duplicating it.
end note

note over CLI
  **Twice, because they land at different
  moments.** The Kit block is the published
  posture; ""-e"" is what sandboxd applies at
  CREATE, which is when sbx would inject. Either
  may lose the race; neither harms when it wins.
end note

note over OP
  **Declining costs no reach today.**
  ""sbx mcp ls"" registers nothing, so the gateway
  aggregates an empty set. ""PROVEO_SBX_MCP=on""
  restores it for an operator with servers of
  their own.
end note

note over SPEC
  **It earns a posture row.** A posture naming
  hosts and credentials but not an MCP server
  the agent is told to call is not describing
  the run. ""posture.MCPGateway"" takes it as a
  VALUE, never re-derives it.
end note
@enduml
